```python
class Bird:
    def fly(self): ...

class Penguin(Bird):
    def fly(self):
        raise NotImplementedError("penguins can't fly")
```
Smell: any code that calls `bird.fly()` polymorphically breaks the moment it receives a `Penguin` — the subclass can't honor the base contract. Fix: `fly()` shouldn't be on `Bird` at all; introduce a `FlyingBird` subtype that only flying birds implement.

